# Competency question (native gmeow:reasoningLogic lane): "Does the boundary square-zero
# law, evaluated as a real first-order logic:Formula over a concrete simplicial triangle,
# ENTAIL that the two intermediate edges of a codimension-2 diamond are a cancelling
# pair?"  Firing math:boundarySquareZeroLaw over the pre-reified incidence atoms of the
# triangle DERIVES the binary consequent math:cancellingPairRel(edgeAB, edgeAC) — the two
# edges composing faceABC to vertexA with opposite sign products. That triple exists in
# the reasoned closure ONLY because the law fired; nothing asserts it. VALUES pins the
# query to edgeAB so the answer is exactly one row {edgeAB, edgeAC}. Removing the law
# formula makes the answer empty.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX excc: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/chain-complex/>

SELECT ?b ?bp WHERE {
    VALUES ?b { excc:edgeAB }
    ?b math:cancellingPairRel ?bp .
}
